.TH "ROARK\-DASHBOARD\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-dashboard-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-dashboard\-create \- Create a dashboard
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark dashboard create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Creates a dashboard with its widgets. Each widget is an analytics query (see POST /v1/analytics/query) with a name unique on the dashboard, a `display` (LINE, NUMBER, RADAR, STACKED_BAR, TABLE) and a `size` (SMALL, MEDIUM, LARGE, EXTRA_LARGE). Widgets render top to bottom in the order given. Dashboard `filters` apply over every widget and must be conversation\-level: AGENT_PROPERTY, CALL_PROPERTY, MODALITY, DATASET or METRIC_VALUE. On a field a widget already filters, the dashboard's wins.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/dashboard
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-time\-range\fR \fI<value>\fR
The window: LAST n DAYS/WEEKS/MONTHS up to now, a CALENDAR_ALIGNED period (TODAY, YESTERDAY, THIS_WEEK, LAST_WEEK, THIS_MONTH, LAST_MONTH, THIS_YEAR, LAST_YEAR), FIXED from/to, or SINCE a date. At most 731 days (two years). Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-filters\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-is\-default\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-widgets\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
